{"findings":[{"title":"Fallback logging keeps the wrong global session id","category":"bug","severity":"low","confidence":"high","evidence":[{"path":"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go","startLine":121,"endLine":132,"symbol":"Init","quote":"logger = createLogger(os.Stderr, level)
			return nil"},{"path":"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go","startLine":135,"endLine":138,"symbol":"Init","quote":"currentSessionID = sessionID"},{"path":"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go","startLine":222,"endLine":248,"symbol":"TestInit_FallsBackToStderrOnError","quote":null}],"reasoning":"Init documents that a non-empty sessionID is stored on every log line, but currentSessionID is only assigned on the successful file-backed path. If creating the log directory or opening entire.log fails, Init returns a working stderr logger with either an empty session_id on first initialization or a stale session_id from a previous Init. That makes fallback logs unfilterable or misattributed exactly when diagnostics are needed most.","reproduction":"Call Init(ctx, "old-session") successfully, then arrange .entire/logs/entire.log to be a directory and call Init(ctx, "new-session"). A subsequent Info(ctx, ...) logs through stderr with currentSessionID still set to "old-session".","recommendation":"Assign currentSessionID = sessionID before any fallback return after validation, or use a small helper that installs logger/currentSessionID together for both stderr and file-backed loggers.","whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis":"TestInit_FallsBackToStderrOnError only checks that Init returns nil and Info does not panic; it does not capture stderr or assert the session_id field on fallback output.","suggestedRegressionTest":"Extend TestInit_FallsBackToStderrOnError to initialize one session successfully, force the fallback path with a different session ID, capture stderr, and assert the emitted JSON contains the new session_id and not the old one.","minimumFixScope":"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go Init fallback branches plus logger fallback coverage in cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go"},{"title":"Close leaves logger pointing at a closed buffered writer","category":"data-loss","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"path":"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go","startLine":135,"endLine":138,"symbol":"Init","quote":"logBufWriter = bufio.NewWriterSize(f, 8192)
	logger = createLogger(logBufWriter, level)"},{"path":"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go","startLine":146,"endLine":159,"symbol":"Close","quote":null},{"path":"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go","startLine":264,"endLine":289,"symbol":"log","quote":"if l == nil {
		l = slog.Default()
	}"}],"reasoning":"Close flushes and closes logBufWriter/logFile and nils those globals, but it does not clear logger. The slog handler created in Init still owns the old bufio.Writer, so any logging after Close uses a handler backed by a closed file instead of falling back to slog.Default. Because the package-level log functions do not return write errors, those post-Close log records are silently dropped.","reproduction":"Call Init(ctx, "session"), then Close(), then Info(context.Background(), "after close"). The logger global is still non-nil, so log uses the stale handler rather than slog.Default; the record is not written to the file and no error is surfaced.","recommendation":"Set logger = nil in Close after closing the file, or replace it with a stderr/default logger if post-Close logging should remain explicitly supported. Add a regression test that logs after Close and verifies it goes to the expected fallback sink instead of the closed file-backed handler.","whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis":"TestClose_SafeToCallMultipleTimes only verifies that repeated Close calls do not panic; it never emits a log after Close or checks that the logger state no longer references the closed writer.","suggestedRegressionTest":"Add a test that installs a file-backed logger, closes it, then logs again with a captured default/stderr logger or reinitialization expectation, asserting the post-Close record is not silently lost through the closed bufio.Writer.","minimumFixScope":"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go Close state reset plus one logger_test.go post-Close behavior test"}],"inspected":{"files":["cmd/entire/cli/logging/context.go","cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go","cmd/entire/cli/logging/context_test.go","cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go","cmd/entire/cli/agent/types/agent.go","cmd/entire/cli/paths/paths.go","cmd/entire/cli/paths/transcript.go","cmd/entire/cli/paths/worktree.go","cmd/entire/cli/validation/validators.go"],"symbols":["WithSession","WithParentSession","WithToolCall","WithComponent","WithAgent","SessionIDFromContext","ParentSessionIDFromContext","ToolCallIDFromContext","ComponentFromContext","AgentFromContext","Init","Close","resetLogger","createLogger","parseLogLevel","isValidLogLevel","Debug","Info","Warn","Error","LogDuration","log","attrsFromContext","ValidateSessionID","WorktreeRoot"],"notes":["Reviewed the owned logging package files and the linked tests as evidence of intended behavior.","Did not run the full test suite; this was a source review of the supplied feature scope."]}}
